---
import Chapter from '../Chapter.astro';
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';
import FigCapabilities from '../figures/FigCapabilities.astro';

const removed = [
  ['The bridge CA', 'The federation falls: there is no path between domains.'],
  ['The cross-certificates', 'The federation falls: the hierarchies are isolated again.'],
  ['The trust list', 'Verifiers are left without anchors.'],
  [
    'PolarisChain',
    'Nothing in the federation falls. Certificates stay signed and any RFC 5280 validator still works. The only loss is knowing what each certificate enables and being able to choose among the paths.',
  ],
];

const caps = [
  {
    name: 'Govern',
    cls: 'govern',
    text: 'Before a cross-certificate is signed, or a policy changes: which certificates become admissible and which stop being so, for the issuer and for third parties that trust its anchors.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Discover',
    cls: 'discover',
    text: 'Inside the handshake: whether an admissible path exists for the presented certificate from an anchor the receiver accepts and, if there are several, which one it prefers.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Audit',
    cls: 'audit',
    text: 'After the decision: not another verdict but its reason, one of seven defined outcomes, with a record that reproduces it.',
  },
];
---

<Chapter id="proposal" num="4" kicker="The proposal" title="A formal model of the federation, not another federation">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Polaris is not on the ship’s route; it is a fixed reference outside it, from which navigators compute their own position. PolarisChain plays the same role, since <strong>it establishes no trust
      relationship</strong> and only reads the ones that others established by issuing certificates, which it turns into a graph and computes over.
      <span class="sn sn--key"
        ><b>Key idea</b> PolarisChain is a formal model of the federation that the domains have already built, and therefore not a fifth federation model beside the other four.</span
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      A bridge, a mesh and a trust list are ways of building roads between domains. PolarisChain is
      the map of the roads that already exist, with precise rules for which ones may be taken and
      which one to take. For this reason it works the same over a mesh, a bridge or trust lists, since it describes those models and does not compete with any of them.
      <span class="sn"
        ><b>The precision the image needs.</b> Once the decision moves into the handshake, each
        domain’s own engine is on the critical path of its own admissions. Two properties still hold, because no domain’s decision is taken by an instance it does not operate and no third party can make it admit a certificate.</span
      >
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="key">PolarisChain computes over the trust that the federation has already established, and adds none of its own.</p>

  <table class="tbl removed">
    <caption><b>Table 2.</b> Remove each component and see what falls.</caption>
    <tbody>
      {
        removed.map(([what, effect], i) => (
          <tr class={i === removed.length - 1 ? 'is-us' : ''}>
            <th scope="row">{what}</th>
            <td>{effect}</td>
          </tr>
        ))
      }
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="prose after">
    <p>
      From that single object follow three computable capabilities, and each of them is <strong>a question put to the same graph</strong>, asked at a different moment and by a different person.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure num={4} class="figure--text fig-caps" caption="Govern, Discover and Audit query the same graph with the same receiver policy. The axis that orders them is time.">
    <FigCapabilities />
  </Figure>

  <div class="caps grid-3">
    {
      caps.map((c) => (
        <div class={`cap cap--${c.cls}`}>
          <h3>{c.name}</h3>
          <p class="small">{c.text}</p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</Chapter>

<style>
  .removed {
    max-width: var(--table);
    margin: 2.6rem 0 0;
  }
  .removed th {
    width: 12rem;
  }
  .removed tr.is-us th {
    color: var(--brass-soft);
  }
  .removed tr.is-us td {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .after {
    margin-top: 4rem;
  }

  .after + :global(.fig-caps) {
    margin-top: 4rem;
  }

  .caps {
    margin-top: 3.4rem;
  }
  .cap {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    border-left: 1px solid;
  }
  .cap .small {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .cap--govern {
    border-color: var(--govern);
  }
  .cap--discover {
    border-color: var(--discover);
  }
  .cap--audit {
    border-color: var(--audit);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .removed th {
      width: 9rem;
      padding-right: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
